# Case 1: the DES Y3 joint xi/Map3 analysis on the observed (unblinded) data, matched to the published setup where the project allows it.
# xi rows follow the DES Y3 cosmic-shear scale cuts (upstream_cosmosis/des-y3-scale-cuts.ini): 227 of 400 xi rows and all 80 Map3 rows enter the chi2.
# Percival t-likelihood with the 796-simulation covariance and parameter_count 16, the published analysis's sampled count (it also samples mnu).
# No compression yet: the published analysis compresses the cut xi block to 16 MOPED modes; set compression_file once that matrix is confirmed.
# For the simulated-analysis check, set data_file = des_y3_sim.datavector (the released simulated measurement at the CosmoGrid cosmology).
# Source n(z): the recorded demonstration processing of the released nz_source table (0.04 per cent of the bin-1 area clipped).
# Priors differ from the published analysis by design: 10^9 A_s sampled uniformly (sigma8 derived), mnu = 0.06 fixed.
# scripts/convert_desy3_fits.py writes every data/ input named here from the released FITS files.

data_file = des_y3_real.datavector
mask_file = des_y3_xi_scale_cut.mask
compression_file =
mock_count = 796
parameter_count = 16
source_ntomo = 4
n_theta = 20
theta_min_arcmin = 2.5
theta_max_arcmin = 250.0
map3_radii_arcmin = 7.0 14.0 25.0 40.0
nz_source_file = des_y3_source.nz
nz_source_bin_width = 0.01
cov_file = des_y3_joint.cov
